  "query_preview": "..\n(Saturday Night through next Friday)\nIssued at 1100 AM CDT Fri Aug 7 2026\n\nA strong Bermuda high will be centered off to our east with\nanother strong high centered over the southwest states. These high\npressure systems will bridge over our area bringing slightly\nhotter temperatures and lower rain chances for Sunday through at\nleast Tuesday. Rain chances will be in the 10 to 30 percent range\nwhile temperatures warm into the low to mid 90s for areas west of\nthe Plateau. Heat risk will climb solidly into the \"Major\" level,\nwhich is level 3 out of 4. It is uncertain if heat headlines will\nbe posted, but Monday and Tuesday look like the days with \ngreatest chances for heat index values topping 105 in parts of \nthe Mid State. \n\nLater in the week, the \"bridge\" between the high pressure centers\nwill flatten out, allowing temps to back off slightly as daily\nshower and storm chances increase. This means generally typical\nAugust heat and humidity with 30 to 50 percent rain chances.",
